{"actor":"Joshua Oliphant","comment":null,"created_at":"2026-03-24T15:19:46Z","event_type":"status_changed","id":36,"issue_id":"brooklet-9f3","new_value":"{\"status\":\"in_progress\"}","old_value":"{\"id\":\"brooklet-9f3\",\"title\":\"CLI: --stream-dir option for plugin subcommands\",\"description\":\"Plugin subcommands (scout scan, pytest scan) don't inherit the --stream-dir option from core commands. The --output flag on scout uses brooklet.open(path) where path is the sessions directory, not a user-chosen stream dir. Plugins should accept --stream-dir so produced topics go to a predictable location.\",\"status\":\"open\",\"priority\":3,\"issue_type\":\"feature\",\"owner\":\"joshua.oliphant@hey.com\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-24T22:11:10Z\",\"created_by\":\"Joshua Oliphant\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-24T22:11:10Z\"}"}
{"actor":"Joshua Oliphant","comment":null,"created_at":"2026-03-24T15:26:12Z","event_type":"closed","id":37,"issue_id":"brooklet-9f3","new_value":"Implemented in PR #5 — both scout and pytest plugins now accept --stream-dir","old_value":""}
{"actor":"Joshua Oliphant","comment":null,"created_at":"2026-03-24T16:31:29Z","event_type":"status_changed","id":38,"issue_id":"brooklet-5nu","new_value":"{\"status\":\"in_progress\"}","old_value":"{\"id\":\"brooklet-5nu\",\"title\":\"CLI: brooklet version command\",\"description\":\"Add a --version flag or version subcommand that prints the installed brooklet version. Basic CLI hygiene.\",\"status\":\"open\",\"priority\":4,\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"owner\":\"joshua.oliphant@hey.com\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-24T22:11:12Z\",\"created_by\":\"Joshua Oliphant\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-24T22:11:12Z\"}"}
{"actor":"Joshua Oliphant","comment":null,"created_at":"2026-03-24T16:31:30Z","event_type":"status_changed","id":39,"issue_id":"brooklet-o5l","new_value":"{\"status\":\"in_progress\"}","old_value":"{\"id\":\"brooklet-o5l\",\"title\":\"CLI: brooklet cat command — read without advancing offsets\",\"description\":\"Add a cat subcommand that dumps a topic's raw JSONL without offset tracking. Currently the only way to read is consume with a throwaway group name, which permanently advances offsets. cat would be read-only inspection, like Unix cat vs tail -f.\",\"status\":\"open\",\"priority\":3,\"issue_type\":\"feature\",\"owner\":\"joshua.oliphant@hey.com\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-24T22:11:12Z\",\"created_by\":\"Joshua Oliphant\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-24T22:11:12Z\"}"}
